      "message": "This does break PELT since the task utilization is already accounted in the blocked load, thus with this patch we are double accounting it.\n\nMoreover, the variable naming \"task_util_boosted\" is misleading and confusing, since in the PELT case we are adding the _non_ boosted utilization (line 6622 above).\n\nFinally, even in the WALT case, why should we use the boosted task utilization?\nSchedTune boost has never been used to define a CPU overvaluation just because it does not make sense.\n\nOverutilization is defined by the actual CPU bandwidth _without_ considering the boost margin. This allows for example to run a small task at the max OPP without (correctly) considering that CPU as overutilized.",
